<%# One page of a conversation, oldest first. The sentinel sits above the entries
    it precedes, so a reader who scrolls to the top is handed the page before
    this one in the same place — the older page is inserted where the sentinel
    stood, with a sentinel of its own on top, and the order of the thread never
    changes.

    The sentinel carries the address and nothing else. What asks for the page is
    the thread's own scroll (see `askForOlderPage` in app.js): htmx's `revealed`
    could not do it here, because it only re-checks on a window scroll and this
    shell scrolls `#thread`.

    It carries no words either. Scrolling up should feel like the conversation
    simply goes on, not like a control was found and pressed, so this is a pixel
    of invisible height rather than a line of text announcing itself. -%>
<% if more -%>
<div class="history-more" data-history-url="<%= h(older_url) %>"></div>
<% end -%>
<% entries.each do |msg| -%>
<%# The entry a search result landed on. The hit names a message; a turn wraps
    several of them, so the entry is what gets marked — and the mark is what
    the browser scrolls to, since an id can only name a message. -%>
<%= View.render("_entry", entry: msg,
                          landed: !landed.nil? && msg.equal?(landed),
                          token_query: token_query,
                          ig_accounts: ig_accounts,
                          ig_linkable_accounts: ig_linkable_accounts,
                          ig_persona: ig_persona) %>
<% end -%>
